      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "I wonder what the goal here is? I presume the same thread/topic is also tracked in private repos such as https://github.com/orgs/bitcoin-security-council/repositories . If the goal is to have a public list of LLM generated issues, that seems fine, but it would be good to tag them with a label like `LLM finding, no external pulls accepted` (or so). Otherwise, there could be a risk that random LLM bots try to send pulls with \"fixes\"?\n\nAgain, not against this. Just wondering about the larger picture and outcome here.",
